const renderCompensationPage = () => `<!doctype html><html lang="en-GB"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">${seoMeta({title:"Housing Disrepair Compensation Guide | Housing Condition Claims UK",description:"Understand how housing disrepair compensation may be assessed, what losses can be considered and what evidence can support a claim.",path:"/housing-disrepair-claims/compensation-calculator/"})}<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Manrope:wght@600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/brand.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/service.css"><style>${baseStyles}${menuStyles}</style><script type="application/ld+json">${JSON.stringify({"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","name":"Housing Disrepair Compensation Guide","url":absoluteUrl("/housing-disrepair-claims/compensation-calculator/"),"about":"Housing disrepair compensation"})}</script></head><body>
<div class="topbar">Housing Condition Claims UK is an official trading style of Sheldon Davidson Solicitors Limited · Authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority · SRA No. 519502</div><nav class="nav wrap"><a class="brand" href="/"><img class="brand-logo" src="/assets/housing-condition-claims-logo.png" alt="Housing Condition Claims UK"><span class="brand-caption">An official trading style of Sheldon Davidson Solicitors Limited</span></a><div class="navlinks"><a href="/housing-disrepair/">Housing claims</a><a href="/faqs">FAQs</a>${megaMenu}<a class="btn dark" href="tel:03339993902">0333 999 3902</a></div><a class="btn dark mobile" href="tel:03339993902">Call us</a></nav>
<main><header class="service-hero"><div class="wrap service-hero-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Housing disrepair compensation</span><h1>How might a housing condition claim be valued?</h1><p class="service-lead">There is no automatic calculator or guaranteed figure. Compensation depends on the particular defects, how long they continued after notice, their effect on the home and the evidence supporting any loss.</p><div class="service-actions"><a class="btn" href="/#callback">Request an individual assessment →</a></div></div><aside class="service-check"><strong>A guide—not a valuation</strong><p>The information below explains common parts of a claim. A solicitor must review the facts and evidence before advising on potential value.</p></aside></div></header>
<section class="service-section wrap"><div class="service-split"><div><span class="eyebrow">The main components</span><h2>What compensation can take into account</h2><p>A housing condition claim may include more than one form of loss. The available heads of loss and method of assessment depend on the legal basis and evidence.</p></div><div class="claim-parts"><article><b>01</b><h3>Loss of use and enjoyment</h3><p>The seriousness, duration and effect on rooms or essential facilities may be considered.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Financial losses</h3><p>Damaged belongings, additional energy, cleaning or accommodation costs may be relevant when reasonable and evidenced.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Health effects</h3><p>Physical or psychological injury may require medical evidence and is assessed separately on its facts.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="service-band"><div class="wrap service-copy-grid"><article><span class="eyebrow">What affects value?</span><h2>Every claim turns on its own evidence.</h2><p>Important considerations can include severity, duration after the landlord was notified, the parts of the home affected, household vulnerability, repair attempts and the conduct of both parties.</p></article><article class="service-council-card"><span class="service-label">Important</span><h2>Do not rely on a headline figure.</h2><p>Percentage bands and examples cannot account for causation, legal responsibility, tenancy terms, expert findings or the quality of the evidence.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="service-section wrap"><div class="service-split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Illustrative method</span><h2>A simplified example</h2><p>If one or more rooms were materially affected for a proven period, legal advisers may examine the rent paid during that period and assess the reduction in use and enjoyment. Supported financial losses may then be considered separately.</p><p class="guide-note">This explanation is illustrative only. It is not a calculation, quotation or prediction of compensation.</p></div><div class="comp-card"><strong>Evidence to collect</strong><ul><li>Dated photographs and videos</li><li>Repair reports and complaint responses</li><li>A clear timeline of notice and recurrence</li><li>Receipts, bills and proof of damaged items</li><li>Inspection, contractor and medical records</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="service-section service-process"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">The assessment process</span><h2>From evidence to legal advice</h2><div class="service-steps"><article><b>01</b><h3>Establish responsibility</h3><p>Identify the defect, its cause and the landlord’s relevant duties.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Establish notice and delay</h3><p>Review when the problem was reported and what action followed.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Assess impact and loss</h3><p>Consider use of the home, evidenced expenses and any supported injury.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="service-related wrap"><h2>Compensation information by repair type</h2><div class="repair-link-grid">${repairLinks}</div></section><section class="service-final wrap"><div><span class="eyebrow">Individual assessment</span><h2>Find out whether we may be able to help.</h2><p>Tell us about the conditions, when you reported them and how they affected your household.</p></div><a class="btn" href="/#callback">Request a callback →</a></section></main>
<footer class="footer wrap"><div class="footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/"><img class="brand-logo" src="/assets/housing-condition-claims-logo.png" alt="Housing Condition Claims UK"><span class="brand-caption">An official trading style of Sheldon Davidson Solicitors Limited</span></a></div><div><strong>Explore</strong><p><a href="/housing-disrepair/">Housing claims</a><br><a href="/#funding">Funding & costs</a><br><a href="/faqs">FAQs</a></p></div><div><strong>Contact</strong><p><a href="tel:03339993902">0333 999 3902</a><br>219 Bury New Road<br>Whitefield, Manchester<br>M45 8GW</p></div></div><small>Housing Condition Claims UK is an official trading style of Sheldon Davidson Solicitors Limited. Sheldon Davidson Solicitors Limited is authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority, SRA No. 519502. Registered in England and Wales, company no. 06958532. Information on this website is general information and not a substitute for legal advice. Representation is subject to individual assessment, written acceptance and agreed terms.</small></footer></body></html>`;

