  return specialDocument({title,description,path,robots:"noindex,follow",schema,body:`<main>${breadcrumbs(crumbs)}<header class="service-hero"><div class="wrap service-hero-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Website enquiries</span><h1>Privacy notice</h1><p class="service-lead">This notice explains how Sheldon Davidson Solicitors Limited uses information submitted through the Housing Condition Claims UK enquiry form.</p></div><aside class="service-check"><strong>Data controller</strong><p>Sheldon Davidson Solicitors Limited, 219 Bury New Road, Whitefield, Manchester, M45 8GW. Email: <a href="mailto:info@sds-solicitors.com">info@sds-solicitors.com</a>.</p></aside></div></header><section class="service-section wrap"><div class="service-split"><div><span class="eyebrow">What we collect</span><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>The form collects your name, email address, telephone number, postcode and selected type of disrepair. Providing this information is voluntary, but without the required details we may be unable to assess or respond to your enquiry.</p></div><div><span class="eyebrow">Why we use it</span><h2>Assessment and contact</h2><p>We use the information to review your housing-condition enquiry, contact you using the details supplied and decide whether the regulated firm may be able to help. We do not use form submissions for unrelated marketing without an appropriate lawful basis.</p></div></div></section><section class="service-band"><div class="wrap service-copy-grid"><article><span class="eyebrow">Lawful bases</span><h2>How processing is justified</h2><p>We rely on taking steps at your request before a possible contract and our legitimate interests in responding to enquiries, administering the service, protecting its security and establishing or defending legal claims. We may also process information where necessary to meet legal or regulatory obligations.</p></article><article class="service-council-card"><span class="service-label">Sharing</span><h2>Who may receive it</h2><p>Access is limited to authorised firm personnel and secure service providers acting on our instructions. We may disclose information to regulators, law-enforcement bodies or others where law or professional obligations require it. If a provider processes information outside the UK, appropriate safeguards will be used where required.</p></article></div></section><section class="service-section wrap"><div class="service-split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Retention</span><h2>How long information is kept</h2><p>Enquiry information is retained only for as long as reasonably necessary to assess and follow up the enquiry, meet regulatory or legal obligations and establish or defend legal claims. It is then deleted or anonymised in accordance with the firm’s retention arrangements.</p></div><div><span class="eyebrow">Your rights</span><h2>Access and control</h2><p>Depending on the circumstances, you may ask for access, correction, erasure or restriction and may object to processing based on legitimate interests. The form is not used to make solely automated decisions about you.</p><p>Contact <a href="mailto:info@sds-solicitors.com">info@sds-solicitors.com</a> to exercise your rights. You may also complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/data-protection-complaints/data-protection-complaints/" rel="noopener">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.</p></div></div></section><section class="service-section service-process"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Further information</span><h2>Firm-wide privacy information</h2><p class="section-intro">This form-specific notice should be read alongside the firm’s wider <a href="https://www.sds-solicitors.com/about-us/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>. Submitting an enquiry does not create a solicitor-client relationship or a contract. Representation depends on an individual assessment, verification and conflict checks, written acceptance and agreed terms.</p></div></section></main>`});
